Explanation:
--------------

RESTORED: OptimizeMemoryForLargeTensors(1 << 20) is re-enabled.

This was previously commented out because it caused the delegate to reject
the graph ("only supports static-sized tensors"). The root cause was that
HasDynamicTensorImpl in subgraph.cc treated all kTfLiteDynamic tensors as
having dynamic shapes, conflating dynamic allocation (memory strategy) with
dynamic shapes (unknown dimensions).

The companion fix in patch 12 modifies HasDynamicTensorImpl to only flag
tensors with truly unknown dimensions (dims contains -1), not those merely
dynamically allocated for memory optimization. With that fix in place,
OptimizeMemoryForLargeTensors can be safely re-enabled -- large activations
get dynamic allocation (avoiding arena OOM) without blocking the delegate.
